coins to a fresh offline wallet and back up the new one.␀␀␀SHOW THE WORDS␀␀VERIFY MY COPY␀␀show this QR to the app that will watch this wallet␀SHOW IT TO␀␀then prove it: RECEIVE > VERIFY - scan the
app's first address to confirm it's yours.
first time? practice with a tiny send first.␀␀Sparrow + more␀␀BlueWallet + more␀␀␀DESKTOP␀MOBILE␀␀on TESTNET␀␀ADDRESS  #%u␀␀␀␀m/%dh/%dh/0h/0/%u   %s␀␀%02x%02x%02x%02x%d%d␀␀␀␀this address was made on the device. trust what you see here, not your computer screen.␀RECEIVE␀ï±  already used
reusing links your coins␀␀FRESH␀␀␀VERIFY: scan an address your computer shows
and this device says if it is really yours␀␀ï“␀ï” NEXT␀␀␀␀VERIFY␀␀bitcoin:␀␀␀␀change address #%u - your coordinator uses these internally␀receive address #%u - safe to give out or send to␀␀␀SCAN ANOTHER␀␀␀␀checked on this device, against this wallet's own keys␀␀VERIFY ADDRESS␀␀ï€Œ  THIS ADDRESS IS YOURS␀␀ï€  NOT THIS WALLET'S␀␀not among this wallet's first 200 receive or change addresses.
it could be another address type or network setting, a different
wallet, or malware swapping addresses on your computer.
do not send to it until you know whose it is.␀␀␀YOUR COORDINATOR WALLET␀the wallet app on your computer or phone (Sparrow, for
example). it watches your balance and builds each
transaction, but cannot sign it on its own.

it shows the tx as a QR (often moving - hold steady).
this device signs, then shows a QR back to the app.␀WHY FLAGGED␀HIGH FEE: the fee is a big share of what you send.
check the rate is what you meant to pay.

␀␀␀TINY COIN IN: you are spending a very small coin.
it may have been sent to track you (a dust attack);
spending it can link your addresses together.

␀␀␀TINY CHANGE: this leaves a very small change coin.
it fragments your balance and can be used to track
you across payments.

␀␀␀␀unsure? go BACK, then in your coordinator
(Sparrow / BlueWallet) freeze or label the coin
and rebuild the transaction without it.␀␀␀REPLACEABLE (RBF)␀␀␀FINAL␀␀␀RBF = Replace-By-Fee. if this transaction gets stuck
unconfirmed, it can be re-sent with a higher fee to
speed it up. a normal, standard setting - most
wallets turn it on by default.

it does NOT change where your coins go, only whether
the fee can be bumped later.␀␀␀this transaction is final: it cannot be re-sent with a
higher fee later (the opposite of RBF). if it gets
stuck, you wait it out.

it does NOT change where your coins go.␀␀part %d of %d␀␀␀single QR␀␀␀SIGN FAILED␀get the transaction from your coordinator␀␀␀SCAN QR␀FROM SD CARD␀␀␀␀point the camera at the QR your
coordinator wallet shows␀␀␀␀or load a .psbt file saved on a card␀␀␀␀the transaction could not be signed␀could not encode the signed transaction␀signed successfully. scan this with your coordinator to broadcast␀␀␀SIGNED␀␀ï€Œ  SIGNED␀this device never touched the network␀␀␀EASY SCAN␀␀␀phone won't catch it? bigger dots,
